// elimination_fine_triangle.vo.expected: expected VO derived by hand from doc/formal (ir_vo.tex WF-VO-*,
// passes.tex I1-I5 and the planner O-/S-/R- rules), independently of the producer.
// Every step is preceded by the rule that fixes its position; RULE GAP marks a position the rules leave open,
// with the tie-break used.
// Planner elimination,fine: "fine enumerates the reversed elimination order" (facade table) = MCS order a,b,c.
// c0=R(a,b), c1=S(b,c), c2=T(c,a)
// RULE GAP (elimination order): passes.tex:333-334 says only "reverse maximum-cardinality search on the primal
// graph, with connected-ready variables or binders first"; the MCS start vertex and tie-break are unstated.
// Derivation assumes MCS ties broken by first written occurrence of the variable; this is an assumption, not a
// rule.
// RULE GAP (O-Fine): "first eligible remaining variable" and "first holding atom" are not ordered by any rule.
// Derivation reads the variable sequence as the heuristic order of first introduction and "first holding atom"
// as the least holding atom under the planner rank at the current B; written position last (I4).
struct Triangle ; relation R (first : i32 [0] , second : i32 [0]) ; relation S (first : i32 [0] , second : i32 [0]) ; relation T (first : i32 [0] , second : i32 [0]) ; answer (a , b , c) : - R (a , b) , S (b , c) , T (c , a) ;
valuation {
    // fineStep(a): holders c0 (e=1), c2 (e=0), both disconnected -> c2 by S-Elimination rank
    T @ 2 (_ , a) ;
    // introduce(a): check of other holder c0
    R @ 0 (a , _) ;
    // fineStep(b): holders c0 (connected via a) and c1 (disconnected) -> c0
    R @ 0 (a , b) ;
    // introduce(b): check of other holder c1
    S @ 1 (b , _) ;
    // fineStep(c): c1 (e=0) and c2 (e=0) both connected -> written c1
    S @ 1 (b , c) ;
    // introduce(c): check of other holder c2; full row
    T @ 2 (c , a) ;
}
